Z||000000||Philphine||05-31-2001||10:25 PM||||i'll pull out mine haynes this weekend when i actually try to do this, but dose anyone know off hand a good place to tap off for an outside third brake light. i guess if i use one stop light or the other it will work and blink with that side. i can try running from the inside 3rd brake light (blocked from view by indy scoop) but if i can get it with out running from the inside out it seems like it would be better. thanks for any help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||cadaver||05-31-2001||10:49 PM||||I think you have to get it from the inside as with a notch there is no brake only signal to the back. The wires run under the carpet on the driver side. Oh wait there is a signal if its a later car. Since these came as GT's as well. It will be in the connector for the lights. Its near the battery.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||06-01-2001||08:08 AM||||Yes, you should be able to tap off of C500, the big engine wiring distribution center there by the battery.  I dont know if the Haynes manual will have these schmatics in detail.  What year is your car?  I have an 87 Helm manual and I can scan some images if you want.<P>I dont know where you'd want to mount the new one, but if you have a wing, I bet you can find a nice one that will mount underneat it.  That way, you can run the wire up through the decklid with the other decklid release, AJAR switch lights.  You could even hide it in the loom that runs from C500 along the firewall and then into the decklid, that'd make a very clean install.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||06-01-2001||09:57 AM||||ok, thanks. i have an older haynes which seems to have more wiring diagrams in it (i noticed that when i got a new one for my nephew), so i'll take a look and see if i get enough info. this ones an '87, but hopfully i'll be doing one or two '84's later. i guess i'll need one of those logic boxes (is that what you call them) for them. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||06-01-2001||06:24 PM||||if you try connecting to the actual tail lite wireing, the turn signals will operate it too. since at the back the brake and turn signals are interconneted. I had to run a new wire from brake switch on pedal to my inside tail lites so the amber turn lites on outside would work independant from the brakes. I have Ferrari kit. has 2 red inside lites for tail and brake, 2 outside amber for turn only.||||reg||1
